Branches (wording from docs/superpowers/probes/2026-10-20-heritage-create.md):
  - species;
  - race: `species_name`, `species_numbers`, `example_measure` and
    `inherited` set; overrides as a top-level "no_longer_true";
  - character with a heritage: `heritage_label`, `heritage_numbers` and
    `inherited` set; overrides per fact;
  - anything else (a character with no heritage, a place, lore, an event,
    an item).
`inherited` is `[(label, source_name, category, text)]`.

Every branch asks for the thing's "aka" and the "names" its facts use,
and gets the context blocks (wording from
docs/superpowers/probes/2026-10-21-connections.md, "Recommended prompt
text"): `mentions` is `[(lead, text)]` and `about` `[(label, facts)]`, a
stub's "Mentioned elsewhere" and "About those"; `named` is
`[(written, label, facts)]`, "Named in this prompt". A label carries the
entry's everyday name: "Tsardom of Moscavia (place, usually called
Moscavia)".

A character gets the homes block: `homes` is `[(heading, about,
[(label, line)])]`, the entries it may be filed in (picked or found in the
prompt, mentioning a stub being expanded, or what a picked place is filed
in) each with its items -- its own facts, then what's filed in it --
labelled S1...; its "in" items then carry "exceptions" (Spheres Task 6's
wording, moved from the gone "ties" onto "in"). An entry shown there isn't
also "Named in this prompt".

Filing (wording from docs/superpowers/probes/2026-10-23-filing.md, probe 1
v1, with v2's names-rule parenthesis and v2's belief rule, ruling F9):
every branch with `nearby` -- the entries near this one (filing nearness,
ruling F6), each "Name (kind, tag; usually called X; in A (role), B;
stub): its summary or first fact" -- gets "in" and "file_into" in its
example object and their rules; every branch but species and race asks
for its "tag", with or without `nearby` (Filing Task 12: a prompt that
names no entry has no near list, and without the rule the model wrote
the kind, "lore", as its tag), and `tags` (`["city (7)", ...]`) is
the tags in use. `hint` is a prompt hint's text (prompts/templates/world/
hints/). The generic branch also gets the "elsewhere" list and its rules,
verbatim from docs/superpowers/probes/2026-10-22-curation.md, "Wording, if
the owner goes ahead" (create-thing, v3: with the relation-claim rule);
the heritage-character branch doesn't. The probe's held-by rule isn't
here (probe 4 fell back to tagging by hand), though the example carries
"held_by": null as probed. "belief" is offered first in `categories`
under the religion, culture or order hint.
-#}
